$DATUM 307-34-6
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the hydrophilic Passerini reaction: An emulsion of
acetic acid (0.17 mmol), acetaldehyde (~0.8 mmol) and furfuryl isocyanide
(0.17 mmol, 1:4:1 ratio) in 2 mL of liquid was stirred for 5 min at RT in
a 20 mL glass vial or without solvent in a 4 ml glass vial. The organic
mixture were extracted with CD3CN and analyzed by 1H NMR spectroscopy and
gas chromatography. 1H NMR (CDCl3): 1.48 (3H, d, J=6.8Hz, CHCH3), 2.13
(3H, s, CH3COO), 4.46 (2H, d, J=5.4Hz, NHCH2), 5.23 (1H, q, J=6.8Hz,
CHCH3), 6.24(1H, dd, J=3.2, 0.7Hz), 6.33 (1H, dd, J=3.2, 1.9Hz), 6.42
(1H, br. s, NH), 7.37 (1H, dd, J=1.9, 0.7Hz). 13C NMR: 18.0, 21.2, 36.4,
70.7, 107.8, 110.6, 142.5, 150.9, 169.5, 170.3. HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd for
C10H13NO4Na: 234.0742, found: 234.0743.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Organic Synthesis "on Water" vs "on Liquids": A Comparative Analysis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sela, Tal; Vigalok, Arkadi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(7), 1964-1967

