$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Phenol-Induced Ugi-4CR.
To a 1 M solution of the aldehyde (1 mmol) in methanol was added
successively 1.0 equiv of amine, 1.0 equiv of isocyanide, and 1.0 equiv
of phenol under inert atmosphere. The resulting mixture was stirred until
completion (TLC). It was then concentrated in vacuo, and the crude
product was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
2-(N-(4-chloro benzyl)-N-(4-methoxy-2-nitro phenyl)amino)-N-cyclohexyl
butanamideRed oil. Yield (72h at 60°C in MeOH): 98%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400
MHz) δ 7.18-7.15 (m, 3H), 7.09 (d, 1H, J = 2.7 Hz), 7.00 (dd, 1H, J =
8.8, 2.7 Hz), 6.95 (d, 2H, J = 8.1 Hz), 6.84 (d, 1H, J = 8.3 Hz), 4.17
(d, 1H, J = 13.9 Hz), 3.97 (d, 1H, J = 13.9 Hz), 3.88-3.77 (m, 1H), 3.81
(s, 3H), 3.50 (t, 1H, J = 7.1 Hz) , 1.95-1.85 (m, 2H), 1.81-1.68 (m, 4H),
1.66-1.55 (m, 2H), 1.46-1.32 (m, 2H), 1.30-1.17 (m, 2H), 0.89 (t, 3H, J =
7.3 Hz). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100.6 MHz) δ 171.6, 157.1, 149.3, 135.3, 134.5,
133.7, 130.7, 129.0, 128.8, 119.5, 109.3, 70.1, 56.4, 56.4, 48.2, 33.6,
33.4, 25.9, 25.2, 25.1, 23.9, 11.1. IR (thin film) 3377, 2932, 2854,
1666, 1527, 1092 cm-1. MS (DI, CI NH3) m/z 460. HRMS Calcd. for
C24H30ClN3O4 459.1925 , Found 459.1902.
