$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Phenol-Induced Ugi-4CR.
To a 1 M solution of the aldehyde (1 mmol) in methanol was added
successively 1.0 equiv of amine, 1.0 equiv of isocyanide, and 1.0 equiv
of phenol under inert atmosphere. The resulting mixture was stirred until
completion (TLC). It was then concentrated in vacuo, and the crude
product was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
2-(N-((furan-2-yl)methyl)-N-(2-nitro phenyl)amino)-N-cyclohexyl
butanamideYellow oil. Yield (16h at 40°C in MeOH): 97%. 1H NMR (CDCl3,
400 MHz) δ 7.66 (dd, 1H, J = 8.3, 1.8 Hz), 7.46 (td, 1H, J = 7.8, 1.8
Hz), 7.29-7.27 (m, 1H), 7.22-7.16 (m, 2H), 7.07 (d, 1H, J = 8.3 Hz), 6.22
(dd, 1H, J = 3.3, 1.7 Hz), 5.96 (d, 1H, J = 3.3 Hz), 4.28 (d, 1H, J =
15.6 Hz), 4.03 (d, 1H, J = 15.6 Hz), 3.80 (dd, 1H, J = 7.6, 5.3 Hz),
3.77-3.70 (m, 1H), 2.02-1.77 (m, 2H), 1.76-1.56 (m, 4H), 1.42-1.12 (m,
6H), 0.96 (t, 3H, J = 7.3 Hz). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100.6 MHz) δ 170.9, 150.2,
147.2, 142.9, 142.6, 133.1, 126.5, 125.2, 125.1, 110.6, 109.9, 68.1,
48.6, 48.2, 33.9, 33.4, 25.9, 25.1, 25.2, 24.1, 10.8. IR (thin film)
3380, 2936, 2851, 1671, 1524, 1358, 1152 cm-1. MS (DI, CI NH3) m/z 386.
HRMS Calcd. for C21H27N3O4 385.2002, Found 385.1996.
