$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of (tert-butylcarbamoyl)(furan-2-yl)methyl benzoate (25)
Follwing General Procedure II, a mixture of isoO cyanide 13 (40.6mg, 55
μL, 0.49 mmol, 1.0 equiv), benzoic acid (5) (63 mg, 0.5mmol, 1.05 equiv)
and aldehyde 10 (49 mg, 43 μL, 0.5 mmol, 1.05equiv) in CH2Cl2was stirred
for 48 hrs. After removal of solvent and silica gel chromatography, 25
(143 mg, 97%) was obtained as a whitish-brown solid. Data for 25: 1H NMR:
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.09-8.06 (m, 2H, aryl); 7.63-7.57 (m, 1H, aryl);
7.50-7.43 (m, 3H, aryl);6.57 (d, J = 3.2 Hz, 1H, aryl); 6.38 (dd, J =
1.6, 3.2 Hz, 1H, aryl); 6.35 (s, 1H, CH); 6.08 (bs, 1H, NH); 1.40 (s, 9H,
CH3) 13C NMR: (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 171.9, 165.3, 148.7, 143.8, 133.9,
130.4, 130.1, 128.8, 111.5, 110.9, 69.6, 52.1, 28.9 IR: (neat) νmax =
1724, 1692, 1452, 1258, 1107, 709 cm-1 TLC: Rf = 0.54 (EtOAc:Hex 1:2)
LRMS: LC/EIMS calculated for C17H19NO4+ [M+ H]+: 302.1, found: 302.1
HPLC: (+/−)-25 tR 22.7 min (50.7%); tR 27.9 min (49.3 %) (−)-25 tR 23.0
min (5.6%); tR 28.2 min (94.6%) (Diacel Chiralcel OJ 0.46 OR: cm φ x 25
cm, 3% IPA in Hexane, 1 mL/min; isocratic) [α]D22= -22.4° (CHCl3, c =
1.17)
