$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Solvent Procedure Aldehyde 1 (3.0
mmol) and isocyanide 3 (3.3 mmol) were added to the solution of a
carboxylic acid 2 (3.3 mmol) in methylene chloride (3 mL) at room
temperature. The reaction mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for
24 h and then concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by
silica-gel flash chromatography using hexane/ethyl octane 6:4 as an
eluent to afford the corresponding product 4. Compound 4g, yield 96%. mp
44-46 °C. 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 0.94 (d, J= 3.9 Hz, 6H), 1.29 (t,
J=7.1 Hz, 3H), 1.71-1.98 (m, 3H), 2.16 (s, 3H), 4.01-4.05 (m, 2H), 4.22
(q, J= 7.1 Hz, 2H), 5.25-5.52 (m, 1H), 6.71 (s, 1H), 13C NMR (50 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 14.6, 17.4, 19.2, 31.2, 41.5, 62.1, 78.4, 170.1, 170.2,
176.0. Anal, calcd. for C12H21NO5: C, 55.58; H, 8.16; N, 5.40. Found: C,
55.57; H, 8.34; N, 5.38. HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd. for C12H21NO5Na [M +
Na]+: 282.1317. Found: 282.1312.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Passerini reaction, reaction run without solvent gave lower yield
