$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Phenol-Induced Ugi-4CR.
To a 1 M solution of the aldehyde (1 mmol) in methanol was added
successively 1.0 equiv of amine, 1.0 equiv of isocyanide, and 1.0 equiv
of phenol under inert atmosphere. The resulting mixture was stirred until
completion (TLC). It was then concentrated in vacuo, and the crude
product was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
N-Benzyl-2-[(4-chloro benzyl)-(2-nitro phenyl) amino] butyramideYellow
solid. Yield (4h at 40°C in MeOH): 96% 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 7.61 (t,
1H, J = 8.1 Hz), 7.43 (td, 1H, J = 8.1, 1.5 Hz), 7.31-7.05 (m, 11H), 6.89
(d, 1H, J = 8.1 Hz), 4.48 (d, 2H, J = 5.8 Hz), 4.28 (d, 1H, J = 15.3 Hz),
4.11 (d, 1H, J = 15.3 Hz), 3.66 (dd, 1H, J = 8.8, 5.1 Hz), 2.04-1.91 (m,
1H), 1.78-1.66 (m, 1H), 0.91 (t, 3H, J = 7.3 Hz). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100.6
MHz) δ 171.6, 147.0, 142.4, 138.5, 135.2, 135.5, 133.1, 130.1, 129.1,
128.9, 128.2, 127.9, 126.3, 125.7, 124.9, 69.9, 53.9, 48.9, 23.3, 11.6.
IR (thin film) 3293, 2969, 1653, 1521, 1363, 1089 cm-1. MS (DI, CI NH3)
m/z 441, 439. Anal. Calcd. for C24H24ClN3O3: C, 65.82 ; H, 5.52. Found:
C, 65.48 ; H, 5.72. m.p. 82°C.
