$DATUM 67-56-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Aminopyrimidine or
Aminopyridine Derivative Synthesis. To a 1 M solution of carbonyl
compound (1 mmol) in methanol or toluene were added the amine (1.0
equiv), the isocyanide (1.0 equiv), and the hydroxypyrimidine or
hydroxypyridine (1.0 equiv). The resulting mixture was stirred at 60 or
90 °C under an inert atmosphere and concentrated in vacuo. The crude
product was then purified by flash chromatography on silica gel to give
the desired adduct. 2-(N-allyl-N-(5-nitro
pyridin-2-yl)amino)-N-tert-butyl butanamide.Yellow oil. Yield (72h at
60°C in MeOH): 96%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 9.08 (d, 1H, J = 2.5 Hz),
8.24 (dd, 1H, J = 9.3, 2.5 Hz), 6.55 (d, 1H, J = 9.3 Hz), 6.22 (br s,
1H), 5.81 (dddd, 1H, J = 17.2, 10.4, 5.3, 4.3 Hz), 5.26 (dd, 1H, J =
10.4, 0.9 Hz), 5.21 (dd, 1H, J = 17.2, 0.9 Hz), 5.22-5.16 (m, 1H), 4.25
(dd, 1H, J = 17.2, 5.3 Hz), 4.21 (dd, 1H, J = 17.2, 4.3 Hz), 2.15-2.04
(m, 1H), 1.79-1.67 (m, 1H), 1.29 (s, 9H), 0.93 (t, 3H, J = 7.5 Hz). 13C
NMR (CDCl3, 100.6 MHz) δ 169.8, 161.0, 146.0, 136.1, 133.3, 133.2, 118.1,
107.1, 60.8, 51.7, 48.4, 29.1, 22.2, 11.2. I.R. (thin film) 3361, 2973,
2881, 1677, 1592, 1495, 1329, 1295, 1121 cm-1. MS (DI, CI NH3) m/z 320.
HRMS Calcd. for C16H24N4O3 320.1848, Found 320.1845.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Ugi-Siles coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
