$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ugi product 12g. According to General Procedure I, reaction between
alkylated DHP-2-one 11 (100 mg, 0.22 mmol), isobutyraldehyde (30 μl, 0.33
mmol), benzylamine (36 μl, 0.33 mmol) and propionic acid (18 μl, 0.24
mmol) in MeOH (250 μl) afforded after 18 h 12g (144 mg, 0.21 mmol, 95%)
as a white foam as a 47:53 mixture of diastereomers. Column
chromatography was performed with c-hexane/EtOAc 9:1→ 8:2 12g, yield (144
mg, 0.21 mmol, 95%) 1H NMR (500 MHz, 413 K, DMSO): δ (ppm) 8.03 (s, 1H),
7.97 (s, 1H), 7.68-7.63 (m, 4H), 7.43-7.38 (m, 4H), 7.34-7.13 (m, 26H),
6.99-6.94 (m, 6H), 5.65 (d, J= 7.3 Hz, 1H), 5.64 (d, J= 7.3 Hz, 1H), 5.27
(d, J= 7.1 Hz, 1H), 5.26 (d, J= 7.0 Hz, 1H), 4.39 (d, JAB = 16.4 Hz, 1H),
4.33 (d, JAB = 16.4 Hz, 1H), 4.19 (d, JAB = 16.3 Hz, 1H), 4.08 (d, JAB =
16.3 Hz, 1H), 4.05 (d, JAB = 17.1 Hz, 1H), 4.04 (d, JAB = 17.1 Hz, 1H),
3.93 (d, JAB = 17.1 Hz, 1H), 3.91 (d, JAB = 17.1 Hz, 1H), 3.90 (d, J=
10.1 Hz, 1H), 3.86 (d, J= 10.4 Hz, 1H), 2.20-2.14 (m, 3H), 2.11-1.98 (m,
3H), 1.38 (s, 18H), 0.97 (t, J= 7.4 Hz, 3H), 0.95 (t, J= 7.4 Hz, 3H),
0.57 (m, 6H), 0.50 (d, J= 6.5 Hz, 3H), 0.45 (d, J= 6.6 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR
(101 MHz, DMSO, 403K): δ (ppm)5 174.1 (C), 173.9 (C), 169.0 (2 C), 167.6
(C), 167.3 (C), 166.1 (2 C), 138.6 (C), 138.5 (C), 138.3 (2 C), 137.3
(C), 137.0 (C), 133.9 (2 C), 128.3-125.8 (40 CH), 112.1 (CH), 112.0 (CH),
80.9 (C), 80.8 (C), 66.4 (2 CH), 63.1 (C), 63.0 (C), 48.2 (CH2)6, 48.5
(CH2)6, 46.6 (2 CH2), 41.9 (CH), 41.7 (CH), 27.0 (6 CH3), 26.2 (2 CH),
25.9 (CH2), 25.8 (CH2), 18.7 (2 CH3), 18.5 (CH3), 18.3 (CH3), 8.5 (2
CH3); IR (neat): 2974 (w), 1744 (m), 1667 (s), 1495 (m), 1368 (s), 1227
(s), 1152 (s), 758 (m), 696 (s), 525 (m). HRMS (EI, 70 eV): calculated
for C44H49N3O5 (M+) 699.3667, found 699.3691.
