$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the preparation of Ugi
products for Pyrrolidinones and Pyridones: To 1 mmol aldehyde in 2 mL
MeOH, 1 mmol amine is added and it is stirred for 5 min. Then, 1 eq
pyridinium hydrochloride is added in case of sodium salt of β -keto
aldehydes. After that, 1 mmol phosphono acetic acid and 1 mmol isocyanide
are added. The reaction mixture is stirred for a night at room
temperature. For the work up, the solvent is evaporated and 3 mL DCM and
2 mL water are added. The aqueous layer is extracted with 1 mL DCM. The
organic layers are combined and washed twice with 2 mL citric acid (5%),
sat. NaHCO3 solution and brine. The organic layer was dried over Na2SO4
and concentrated in vacuum. The product could be crystallized or
otherwise purified by column or wave chromatography or preparative HPLC.
General procedure for the HWE: To the obtained Passerini product is
diluted in 40mL THF under N2, 4,5eq LiCl were added. The mixture was
stirred at 0° until the complete dissolution of LiCl. Then 10 eq Et3N
were added. The reaction mixture was stirred at 0° for 30 min and then
for 12 h at room temperature. For the work up, the solution was filtered
on SiO2 that was next washed with ethyl acetate and methanol. The solvent
is concentrated in vacuum. The product could be crystallized in ethyl
acetate or otherwise purified by column, wave chromatography or
preparative HPLC.
1-Benzyl-3-biphenyl-4-yl-5-oxo-2,5-dihydro-1H-pyrrole-2-carboxylic acid
tert-butylamide (16): scheduled quantity 1 mmol gave 325 mg (95 %)
C28H28N2O2 MW: 424.54 g/mol; Rf: 0.72 (PE/EA, 1/4, v/v); HPLCMS (ESI): tR
= 3.96 min, m/z = 425.2 [M+H]+, 447.2 [M+Na]+; 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ
= 1.07 (s, 9H, TBU), 4.11-4.15 (d, 1H, 2J=14.86Hz, 1H of NCH2Ph), 4.77
(s, 1H, CHC=CHCO), 5.00-5.04 (d, 1H, 2J=14.86Hz, 1H of NCH2Ph), 5.35 (s,
1H, NH), 6.44 (s, 1H, C=CHCO), 7.18-7.38 (m, 9H, 9xCH-ar), 7.50- 7.59 (m,
5H, 5xCH-ar); 13C-NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz): δ = 28.21 (TBU), 45.11 (NCH2Ph),
51.57 (-C- (CH3)3), 68.69 (CHC=CHCO), 120.28 (C=CHCO), 126.92-128.84
(14xCH-ar), 129.24, 136.54, 139.71, 143.13, 155.29, 165.38 (CO), 171.25
(CO).
