$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure II. Preparation of α-acyloxycarboxamides (Enan). A 25
mL flame dried r.b.f. under argon and equipped with a stir bar was
charged with ≅ 7.0-9.0 mL methylenechloride, Cu(OTf)2 (20 mol %) and
indane (pybox) ligand 4 (20 mol %).1 The mixture was stirred until the
components were completely dissolved (heating the solution to 38 °C was
necessary). Aldehyde (0.40-0.50 mmol) was dissolved and the solution was
cooled to 0 °C and allowed to stand for 30 min at which time AW-300 MS
(molecular sieves ≅ 400 mg) were added. In a separate, dry r.b.f. (under
argon), the acid (0.40-0.50 mmol) and isocyanide (0.40-0.50 mmol, 0.95
equiv) were dissolved in ≅ 3.0 mL of methylenechloride. AW-300 MS (100
mg) were added and the mixture was either shaken or stirred for 30 min.
This mixture was drawn into a gas syringe and delivered to the first
solution via a syringe pump at a rate that ended after 4 h. The reaction
was stirred for 8 to 18 h during which time TLC analysis, using a 1:1,
ethyl acetate:hexanes eluent, was conducted. When the TLC denoted
completion, 2.0 mL of sodium hypochlorite (NaOCl) was added and the
mixture was allowed to stir for a further 1 h. After removal of solvent
under reduced pressure, the crude reaction mixture was applied directly
to a silica gel column. The major product (as denoted by the TLC) was
separated by gradient flash column chromatography (silica gel, 9:1 -1:3
hexanes:ethyl acetate). Synthesis of
1-(4-methoxyphenylcarbamoyl)-2-(benzyloxy)ethyl benzoate (8) Following
General Procedure II, a mixture of isocyanide 7 (60 mg, 0.45 mmol, 1.0
equiv), benzoic acid (5) (58 mg, 0.47 mmol, 1.05 equiv) aldehyde 6 (71
mg, 66 μL, 0.47 mmol, 1.05 equiv) and 20 mol % of catalyst 4 in CH2Cl2was
stirred for 18 hrs. After removal of solvent followed by silica gel
chromatography, 8 (170 mg, 93%)2 was obtained as a white solid. Data for
8: 1H NMR: (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.14-8.12 (dd, J = 1.0, 8.5 Hz, 2H, aryl);
7.92 (bs, 1H, NH); 7.66-7.63 (m, 2H, aryl); 7.52-7.47 (m, 2H, aryl);
7.43-7.40 (m, 2H, aryl); 7.31-7.26 (m, 4H, aryl); 6.86-6.85 (d, J = 8.5
Hz, 2H, aryl); 5.70 (t, J = 4.0, 1H, CH); 4.62 (s, 2H, CH2); 4.07 (dd, J
= 4.5, 6.5 Hz, 1H, CH2); 3.99 (dd, J = 4.5, J = 6.5, 1H, CH2); 3.79 (s,
3H, CH3). 13C NMR: (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 171.3, 163.9, 156.9, 133.9, 131.9,
130.4, 130.2, 129.6, 129.4, 129.0, 128.9, 128.7, 127.9, 127.2, 122.3,
114.5, 73.8, 69.5, 55.7. IR: (neat) νmax = 1726, 1690, 1512, 1246 cm-1
TLC: Rf = 0.30 (silica gel, EtOAc:Hex 1:2) HRMS: EIMS calculated for
C24H23NO5+ [M+ H]+: 406.1655, found: 406.1653 HPLC: (+/−)-8 tR 27.41 min
(48.7%); tR 30.72 min (51.3 %) (+)-8 tR 28.72 min (98.4%); tR 32.23 min
(1.6%) (Daicel Chiralcel OD 0.46 cm φ x 25 cm, 5% IPA in Hexane, 1
mL/min; isocratic) OR:[α]D22= + 17.7° (CHCl3, c = 2.21)
