$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of G0 Hexanedioic acid (0.146 g, 1.00 mmol), a (0.210 g, 2.19
mmol, 9.5% excess) and b (0.260 g, 2.13 mmol, 6.5% excess) and
tetrahydrofuran (THF, 1 mL) were mixed and heated to 40 °C with stirring
in a 25 mL Schlenk flask. Initially, the mixture is heterogeneous, and
the solution turned to clear after being stirred for about 2 h. Finally,
the reaction mixture was precipitated into cold diethyl ether (4 °C)
after stirring for 48 h, and a brown solid was obtained after being dried
under vacuum. A small amount of this compound (0.05g) was further
purified by silica gel column chromatography (ethyl acetate), and 0.044 g
was obtained. The impurity was compound b as confirmed by thin layer
chromatography. This purified compound is designated as G0'. White solid,
yield (0.533 g, yield: 92%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Passerini reaction, Schlenk flask used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Combination of Orthogonal ABB and ABC Multicomponent Reactions toward
Efficient Divergent Synthesis of Dendrimers with Structural Diversity
