$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Experimental Procedure. All three
components were mixed in equimolar amounts (1 mmol) in the IL (1.0-1.5
mL) or PEG 400 (1.0 mL) at r.t. under an argon atmosphere and stirring
was continued until no starting materials could be detected (TLC). The
reaction was then extracted with Et2O (3 × 5 mL) by simple decantation.
The combined organic phases were filtered through a small pad of silica
and concentrated at reduced pressure to furnish the crude products in
high purity (>90% by 1H NMR analysis). Analytical samples were obtained
after column chromatography (30% EtOAc in hexane). Compound 7, yield 91%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry (- solvent), Passerini reaction, multicomponent reaction,
atom economy, polyethylene glycol (PEG400) solvent gave better yield than
ionic liquid [bmim].PF6
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Revisiting the Passerini reaction under eco-friendly reaction conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
