$DATUM Synthesis of (benzylcarbamoyl)(furan-2-yl)methyl benzoate (24) Folling
wing General Procedure II, a mixture of isocyanide 11 (53 mg, 55 μL, 0.45
mmol, 1.0 equiv), benzoic acid (5) (58 mg, 0.5 mmol, 1.05 equiv) and
aldehyde 10 (45 mg, 39 μL, 0.5 mmol, 1.05 equiv) in CH2Cl2was stirred for
48 hrs. After removal of solvent and silica gel chromatography, 24 (135
mg, 90%) was obtained as a white solid. Data for 24: 1H NMR: (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 166.4, 165.1, 148.2, 143.9, 137.8, 134.0, 130.2, 129.1, 129.0,
128.8, 1 28.7, 127.8, 111.9, 111.0, 69.5, 43.7 IR: (neat) νmax = 1724,
1670, 1266, 1093, 1069, 709 cm-1 TLC: Rf = 0.36 (EtOAc:Hex 1:2) LRMS:
LC/EIMS calculated for C20H17NO4+ [M+ H]+: 336.1, found: 336.1 HPLC:
(+/−)-24 tR 31.4 min (50.1%); tR 39.9 min (49.9 %) (−)-24 tR 32.8 min
(12.4%); tR 40.3 min (87.6%) (Diacel Chiralcel OD 0.46 cm φ x 25 cm, 5%
IPA in Hexane, 1 mL/min; isocratic) OR: [α]D22= -12.1° (CHCl3, c = 1.57).
