$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Representative Procedure for the Synthesis of Di-O-acyl-glyceramides.
Compound 20b. A mixture of acetic acid (57 µL, 1.0 mmol) and Cu(acac)2
(2.6 mg, 0.01 mmol, 1 mol %) toluene (2 mL) in a 10 mL round-bottom flask
was heated to 60 °C for 10 min under nitrogen. To it was added dropwise a
solution of diazoketone 1a (226 mg, 1.3 mmol, 1.3 equiv) in toluene (2
mL).Once gas evolution was judged complete, the reaction mixture was
stirred an additional 5 min, then cooled and concentrated in Vacuo. The
oily residue was blanketed in nitrogen, then treated with isobutyric acid
(140 µL, 1.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv) and t-BuNC (170 µL, 1.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv).
The resulting reaction mixture was stirred at rt under N2 for 20 h. The
product was purified by silica gel flash column chromatography (1:1
EtOAc:hexanes, Rf ) 0.3) to afford 5b (338 mg, 90%) as a pale-yellow oil.
